 "rule_text": "PANEL-THINNING TEST (DESIGN \u00a74 panel-density robustness; D17(d)), GBDT_AB_17 on feature set A+B (tb_asym_* excluded), hyper-parameters fixed, no re-tuning, seeds config/seeds.yaml, same folds. Thinned-panel Tier B tables tierB_dmin<c>.parquet, c in {0.03, 0.12, 0.35}, recomputed from the cached panel hits (species with d_s < c removed). Statistic T_pf (per-fold paired dAP vs B1, mean over species) with per-species dAP vs B1. Conditions per c: N->N (incumbent), N->T<c> (train natural, evaluate thinned), T<c>->T<c> (train and evaluate thinned), A<c>->N and A<c>->T<c> (masking augmentation: train on natural plus c-masked copies of each training pair; all copies of a pair in the pair's fold; pair weights (species-balanced, computed on pairs) spread over the pair's unique copies so each pair sums to its pair weight; identical copies deduplicated; min_samples_leaf counted in pairs (x rows/pairs); no early stopping; evaluation on one row per pair). ADOPTION RULE for masking augmentation, decided at c=0.35: adopt iff (1) T_pf(N->N) - T_pf(N->T0.35) > 0 with the 95% percentile paired-bootstrap CI of the drop excluding 0, AND (2) T_pf(A0.35->T0.35) - T_pf(N->T0.35) >= 0.5 x the drop (recovers at least half), AND (3) T_pf(N->N) - T_pf(A0.35->N) <= 0.01 (natural-panel T_pf not lowered by more than 0.01). Point estimates for (2) and (3). c = 0.03 and 0.12 are reported, not decisive.",
